{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":73076,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"1d16f4c9-415f-5a6a-b358-a01781fd9ff4","total_cost_usd":0.669094,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14940,"cache_read_input_tokens":10583,"output_tokens":7090,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2237,"cache_read_input_tokens":10583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4357},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5076,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005170999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7090,"cacheReadInputTokens":10583,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14940,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.663923,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-k2-reviewer-fable-50\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:ef969c57ba5a856f4581\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description names segment_id as the independent-unit column and defines one trial as one row, so the unit-to-row mapping expected by the sign test is one row per independent unit.\",\"observed_value\":{\"independent_unit_column\":\"segment_id\",\"one_trial\":\"one row\"},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Independent unit column: segment_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"}]},{\"description\":\"data/input.csv contains exactly 24 data rows with segment_id values S01 through S24, each appearing exactly once and with all street names distinct; no independent unit contributes more than one row.\",\"observed_value\":{\"n_rows\":24,\"n_unique_segment_ids\":24,\"duplicate_segment_ids\":0,\"duplicate_street_names\":0},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"S01,Alder Row,310,2,58.4,55.0\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"S24,Yarborough Road,570,4,60.5,62.1\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly refuses any input file in which a segment_id repeats, so the row-independent sign test cannot receive multiple rows from the same independent unit.\",\"observed_value\":\"SystemExit raised on duplicate segment_id before the test runs\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"labels = [row[\\\"segment_id\\\"] for row in segments]\\n    if len(set(labels)) != len(labels):\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"segment_id repeats: the sign test needs one row per segment\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The reported trial count equals the number of unique independent units: the sign test is run on 24 trials, and I independently recomputed 18 negative and 6 positive changes from the raw CSV, matching the reported 18-of-24 split and p = 0.022656.\",\"observed_value\":{\"trials\":24,\"quieter\":18,\"louder\":6,\"reported_p\":0.022656},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":42,\"end_line\":42,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Exact two-sided sign test on 24 independent street segments, one paired row each: 18 of 24 segments were quieter after porous asphalt resurfacing (share 0.750, p = 0.022656), with a median change of -1.450 dB(A).\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":29,\"quoted_text\":\"Segments analysed: 24\\nQuieter after resurfacing: 18\\nLouder after resurfacing: 6\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description states there is no grouping column (block, contractor batch, district) that could tie several rows back to a common underlying unit, and no such column exists in the CSV header.\",\"observed_value\":\"no grouping columns present\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":31,\"quoted_text\":\"Nothing\\nin the file marks a larger grouping: there is no shared block, contractor\\nbatch, or district column that would tie several rows back to the same site.\\nStreet names are all distinct, and the identifiers do not repeat.\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"segment_id,street_name,resurfaced_length_m,lanes,pre_lnight_db,post_lnight_db\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Each segment does involve repeated underlying measurements (multiple nights of logging per week, before and after), which could in principle constitute repeated entries from one unit; however, the description states each week was energy-averaged on site into a single number, so only one aggregated pre/post pair per unit enters the analysis and the repetition never reaches the row-independent procedure as separate rows.\",\"observed_value\":\"within-unit repeated measurements pre-aggregated to one value per week\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":19,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"- pre_lnight_db: the L_night noise indicator before resurfacing, in dB(A). The\\n  logger ran for one full week and the whole week was condensed on site into\\n  this single energy-averaged figure, so the file stores one number rather than\\n  the individual nights.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":28,\"quoted_text\":\"Because each week of logging is already averaged into a single number, every\\nsegment supplies exactly one paired row and nothing more, and the number of\\nrows in the file equals the number of independent sites in the study.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I actively tried to demonstrate the issue: I scanned all 24 CSV rows for repeated segment_id values (none; S01-S24 each occur once), checked street_name for repeats that might reveal one street entered under multiple segment IDs (all 24 names are distinct, and the description states no two segments share a carriageway, junction, or corridor), and looked for any auxiliary column that could group multiple rows under one underlying unit (the header has none). I traced the analysis code to confirm the tested trial count is len(changes) built from one change per row with no row duplication, resampling, or per-night expansion, and that a duplicate-ID input would abort before testing. I also recomputed the sign counts from the raw data (18 quieter, 6 louder of 24) and confirmed they match the reported result, so the reported n equals the number of distinct independent units. No route by which a single independent unit enters the sign test more than once could be constructed from the supplied files.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-k2-reviewer-fable-50","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:ef969c57ba5a856f4581","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names segment_id as the independent-unit column and defines one trial as one row, so the unit-to-row mapping expected by the sign test is one row per independent unit.","observed_value":{"independent_unit_column":"segment_id","one_trial":"one row"},"source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: segment_id\nOne trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"data/input.csv contains exactly 24 data rows with segment_id values S01 through S24, each appearing exactly once and with all street names distinct; no independent unit contributes more than one row.","observed_value":{"n_rows":24,"n_unique_segment_ids":24,"duplicate_segment_ids":0,"duplicate_street_names":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"S01,Alder Row,310,2,58.4,55.0"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"S24,Yarborough Road,570,4,60.5,62.1"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly refuses any input file in which a segment_id repeats, so the row-independent sign test cannot receive multiple rows from the same independent unit.","observed_value":"SystemExit raised on duplicate segment_id before the test runs","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"labels = [row[\"segment_id\"] for row in segments]\n    if len(set(labels)) != len(labels):\n        raise SystemExit(\"segment_id repeats: the sign test needs one row per segment\")"}]},{"description":"The reported trial count equals the number of unique independent units: the sign test is run on 24 trials, and I independently recomputed 18 negative and 6 positive changes from the raw CSV, matching the reported 18-of-24 split and p = 0.022656.","observed_value":{"trials":24,"quieter":18,"louder":6,"reported_p":0.022656},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":42,"end_line":42,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Exact two-sided sign test on 24 independent street segments, one paired row each: 18 of 24 segments were quieter after porous asphalt resurfacing (share 0.750, p = 0.022656), with a median change of -1.450 dB(A)."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":27,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"Segments analysed: 24\nQuieter after resurfacing: 18\nLouder after resurfacing: 6"}]},{"description":"The data description states there is no grouping column (block, contractor batch, district) that could tie several rows back to a common underlying unit, and no such column exists in the CSV header.","observed_value":"no grouping columns present","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":28,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"Nothing\nin the file marks a larger grouping: there is no shared block, contractor\nbatch, or district column that would tie several rows back to the same site.\nStreet names are all distinct, and the identifiers do not repeat."},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":1,"quoted_text":"segment_id,street_name,resurfaced_length_m,lanes,pre_lnight_db,post_lnight_db"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Each segment does involve repeated underlying measurements (multiple nights of logging per week, before and after), which could in principle constitute repeated entries from one unit; however, the description states each week was energy-averaged on site into a single number, so only one aggregated pre/post pair per unit enters the analysis and the repetition never reaches the row-independent procedure as separate rows.","observed_value":"within-unit repeated measurements pre-aggregated to one value per week","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":19,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"- pre_lnight_db: the L_night noise indicator before resurfacing, in dB(A). The\n  logger ran for one full week and the whole week was condensed on site into\n  this single energy-averaged figure, so the file stores one number rather than\n  the individual nights."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":26,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"Because each week of logging is already averaged into a single number, every\nsegment supplies exactly one paired row and nothing more, and the number of\nrows in the file equals the number of independent sites in the study."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I actively tried to demonstrate the issue: I scanned all 24 CSV rows for repeated segment_id values (none; S01-S24 each occur once), checked street_name for repeats that might reveal one street entered under multiple segment IDs (all 24 names are distinct, and the description states no two segments share a carriageway, junction, or corridor), and looked for any auxiliary column that could group multiple rows under one underlying unit (the header has none). I traced the analysis code to confirm the tested trial count is len(changes) built from one change per row with no row duplication, resampling, or per-night expansion, and that a duplicate-ID input would abort before testing. I also recomputed the sign counts from the raw data (18 quieter, 6 louder of 24) and confirmed they match the reported result, so the reported n equals the number of distinct independent units. No route by which a single independent unit enters the sign test more than once could be constructed from the supplied files.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":29325,"ttft_stream_ms":1575,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":71416,"uuid":"52384a26-4338-4a86-becf-f7c29d210ddb"}
